---
description: Git-flow workflow rules and branch protection
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---
- This project uses Git-flow workflow for branch management.
- **Always start new work from the `develop` branch.** Before creating any feature/bugfix/release branch, ensure you are checked out to `develop` and it is up to date with `origin/develop`.
- Never commit directly to the `main` branch. Main only receives merges from `develop`.
- Never commit directly to the `develop` branch. Develop only receives merges from feature/bugfix/hotfix/release branches.
- All new work must be done on feature branches: `feature/description`, `bugfix/description`, `hotfix/description`, or `release/X.Y.Z`.
- Feature branches are created from `develop` and merged back to `develop`.
- Bugfix branches are created from `develop` and merged back to `develop`.
- Hotfix branches are created from `main` and merged to both `main` and `develop`.
- Release branches are created from `develop` and merged to both `develop` and `main`.
- When merging a release branch to `main`, the VERSION file is automatically updated and a Git tag is created.
- All commits must follow Conventional Commits format: `type: description` (e.g., `feat: add new feature`, `fix: resolve bug`).
- The pre-commit hook enforces these rules automatically.